    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (50 tests, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `householdId` is now a deterministic function of `(normalizedLastName, postcode)`, computed for every create, and everything that keys off the household reads that computed value.\n\n**`AssignHousehold.java`** \u2014 Now always computes `householdId` = first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` (previously it was lastName+address, only when `sharesHousehold` was set, and it backfilled other owners). No lookup or backfill is needed anymore since every member independently computes the same value. Owners with no postcode get a null `householdId` (no household), matching the existing \"only owners with a postcode participate\" rule.\n\n**`EnsureUniqueIdentity.java`** \u2014 Still rejects full-identity duplicates (the whole `identityKey`, which always applies even with `sharesHousehold`), and now *also* rejects a **household duplicate**: an owner whose computed `householdId` matches an existing owner is a 409 **unless** the request sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared member. This is where `sharesHousehold` now only bypasses the block rather than creating the link.\n\n**`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 A declared household member (`sharesHousehold` true) is never flagged as a suspected duplicate (`possibleDuplicate=false`). A non-declared owner sharing lastName+postcode never reaches this step (it's 409'd upstream), so the soft-match no longer fires spuriously.\n\n**`AssignHouseholdSize.java`** \u2014 No logic change (it already counts by stored `householdId`); updated the javadoc since the value is now deterministic and always set rather than backfilled.\n\nKey test-verified behaviours: same lastName+postcode \u2192 same `householdId` and a 409 without `sharesHousehold` (Cp10, Cp11, Cp36); with `sharesHousehold` \u2192 created, not flagged (Cp35, Cp23); full-identity duplicates still 409 even with `sharesHousehold` (Cp03, Cp25, Cp28).",
